fix: replace ResNet-101 backbone with CTransPath Swin Tiny + FuzzyArcLoss V2

The ABMIL/Choquet checkpoints were trained on CTransPath embeddings, not
ResNet-101. This caused mismatched feature spaces and incorrect predictions.

Changes:
- New CTransPathPipeline: ConvStem(4ch) → Swin Tiny(768d) → Projection(512d)
- Load finetuned backbone from best_fuzzyarcloss_v2.pth (F1=0.939)
- Real tile embeddings from CTransPath now fed to ABMIL/Choquet downstream
- Mount BACKBONES directory (ctranspath.pth + best_fuzzyarcloss_v2.pth)
- Fix frontend bug: image selection drift during job polling
